# D-28 (steps/defects.md, author's reading A): a formal parameter is the
# nearest lexical binding for its own name and shadows a unit-level named
# Structure sharing that spelling -- l2_path_root tried the unit-level
# Structure before the formal since -113, so bump's own formal was never
# seen whenever the unit also declared a Structure of the same name.
#
# The formal is TYPED as Model and NAMED Model (`Model: Model`) -- a type
# comes only from the declaration (no name specials, fable's correction on
# this ticket's first attempt, which had wrongly inferred a shape from an
# untyped formal's own name for the L1-style `@(Lmx x)` spelling instead;
# that spelling stays opaque here on purpose, see unit_addr_arg.lm2 and
# friends for it). `Model\value: 99` inside bump must write through the
# FORMAL (fresh, the argument), not the eternal unit-level Model. make()
# reads both afterward: fresh\value proves the write landed on the
# argument; Model\value proves the eternal Structure's own declared value
# was untouched. Success is nonzero (steps/current.md's witness rule).
Model:
    int: value 1
end: Model

fn: bump (Model: Model) int
    Model\value: 99
    return: Model\value
end: bump

fn: make () int
    Model: fresh
    bump(fresh)
    if: fresh\value != 99
        return: 91
    if: Model\value != 1
        return: 92
    return: 7
end: make

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: make(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
